[1m[38;5;231mWhich change-detection approach should the design commit to?[0m

[38;5;153m❯[39m [38;5;246m1.[39m [38;5;153mA — event log, derive on read (Recommended)[39m
     [38;5;246mImmutable event log as source of truth; notifications and the catch-up view are queries over it. Retroactively [39m
     [38;5;246mre-derivable when you tune the trigger filter. Materialize as a cache later if ever needed.[39m
  [38;5;246m2.[39m B — materialized notification rows
     [38;5;246mWrite a notification record per subscriber on each mutation. Simplest read path. Trigger-rule changes apply only [39m
     [38;5;246mgoing forward, and state is duplicated.[39m
  [38;5;246m3.[39m A now, materialize immediately
     [38;5;246mBuild the event log and also write materialized rows from day one. Belt and braces, more moving parts to keep [39m
     [38;5;246mconsistent than the data volume justifies.[39m
